WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.493
Military chain of command.

00:00:02.443 --> 00:00:04.647
Systematic degradation.

00:00:04.647 --> 00:00:11.613
Between 2015 and 2024, Canada's senior military leadership was systematically dismantled.

00:00:11.613 --> 00:00:14.840
Three Chiefs of the Defence Staff in three years.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:20.079
Vice Admiral Mark Norman prosecuted on breach of trust charges that were ultimately stayed.

00:00:20.079 --> 00:00:28.011
Operation Honour, launched to address sexual misconduct, became a mechanism for removing senior officers while operational readiness collapsed.

00:00:28.011 --> 00:00:35.249
The result: a military that cannot recruit, cannot equip, cannot house its members, and cannot deploy at NATO standards.

00:00:35.249 --> 00:00:39.159
The leadership that built operational capability was replaced.

00:00:39.159 --> 00:00:44.704
What remained was a command structure aligned with political priorities rather than military readiness.

00:00:44.704 --> 00:00:47.102
Vice Admiral Mark Norman.

00:00:47.102 --> 00:00:53.363
The highest-profile politically motivated prosecution of a serving military officer in modern Canadian history.

00:00:53.363 --> 00:01:04.215
Norman, the Vice Chief of the Defence Staff, was charged with breach of trust in 2018 for allegedly leaking cabinet confidences related to the Davie Shipbuilding Resolve-class supply ship contract.

00:01:04.215 --> 00:01:12.806
The prosecution appeared to be retaliation for Norman's advocacy of a procurement decision that had already been approved but was being reversed for political reasons.

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:22.693
After three years of legal proceedings and the disclosure of thousands of government documents, the Crown stayed all charges in May 2019 citing no reasonable prospect of conviction.

00:01:22.693 --> 00:01:25.249
Norman's career was destroyed.

00:01:25.249 --> 00:01:28.443
His legal costs exceeded two million dollars.

00:01:28.443 --> 00:01:31.193
The government eventually paid the costs.

00:01:31.193 --> 00:01:34.749
No one was held accountable for the prosecution itself.

00:01:34.749 --> 00:01:37.329
Chief of the Defence Staff turnover.

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:42.409
An unprecedented period of instability at the top of Canada's military command.

00:01:42.409 --> 00:01:50.931
General Jonathan Vance served as CDS from 2015 to 2021 and was subsequently investigated for sexual misconduct.

00:01:50.931 --> 00:01:58.409
Admiral Art McDonald was appointed CDS in January 2021 and stepped aside within weeks under investigation.

00:01:58.409 --> 00:02:04.397
General Wayne Eyre served as acting and then full CDS from 2021 to 2024.

00:02:04.397 --> 00:02:13.897
Three CDS in three years at a time when the military faced a recruitment crisis, equipment shortfalls, NATO pressure, and the largest personnel deficit in decades.

00:02:13.897 --> 00:02:15.727
Operation Honour.

00:02:15.727 --> 00:02:22.920
Launched in 2015 by General Vance following the Deschamps Report on sexual misconduct in the Canadian Armed Forces.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:28.295
The operation was designed to address a documented culture of sexual harassment and assault.

00:02:28.295 --> 00:02:33.034
However, Operation Honour also became a mechanism for institutional control.

00:02:33.034 --> 00:02:41.431
The reporting structure created new internal processes that operated through the chain of command — meaning complaints flowed through the same leadership structure being accused.

00:02:41.431 --> 00:02:48.204
When the officer who launched Operation Honour was himself investigated, the credibility of the entire initiative collapsed.

00:02:48.204 --> 00:02:53.659
The Arbour Report in 2022 recommended forty-eight reforms, many echoing Deschamps.

00:02:53.659 --> 00:03:00.420
The pattern: launch an initiative, use it to reshape the institution, then the initiative's own architect is removed.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:02.624
The operational result.

00:03:02.624 --> 00:03:09.374
While Canada's military leadership was being systematically disrupted, the military's operational capability collapsed.

00:03:09.374 --> 00:03:13.806
Personnel shortfall: sixteen thousand below authorized strength.

00:03:13.806 --> 00:03:19.579
NATO defence spending: one point two nine percent of GDP against a two percent target.

00:03:19.579 --> 00:03:26.170
Equipment: aging CF-18 fighters, delayed surface combatant ships, submarines unable to deploy.

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:33.079
Housing: military families in substandard Residential Housing Units with mould, pest infestations, and broken heating.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:36.284
Recruitment: more members leaving than joining.

00:03:36.284 --> 00:03:40.590
Veteran care: MAID offered to veterans seeking mental health support.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:44.647
The leadership that would have fought for operational readiness was removed.

00:03:44.647 --> 00:03:49.386
What remained was a command structure focused on compliance rather than capability.

00:03:49.386 --> 00:03:51.886
The architecture of degradation.

00:03:51.886 --> 00:03:55.738
The pattern across TENET5 investigations is consistent.

00:03:55.738 --> 00:04:03.772
Competent leadership that prioritises operational effectiveness is removed through criminal prosecution, investigation, or institutional process.

00:04:03.772 --> 00:04:09.443
The process itself is the punishment — by the time charges are stayed or investigations concluded, the

00:04:09.556 --> 00:04:13.926
officer's career is destroyed and the institutional knowledge is lost.

00:04:13.876 --> 00:04:18.649
The replacements prioritise political alignment over operational capability.

00:04:18.649 --> 00:04:25.694
The result is a military that cannot recruit, cannot equip, cannot house its members, and cannot meet its NATO obligations.

00:04:25.694 --> 00:04:27.876
This is not accidental.

00:04:27.876 --> 00:04:33.058
A military with competent, independent leadership resists unconstitutional orders.

00:04:33.058 --> 00:04:36.580
A military with politically aligned leadership complies.

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:44.444
The Norman prosecution, the CDS turnover, Operation Honour, the equipment crisis, the personnel crisis — they are not separate problems.

00:04:44.444 --> 00:04:51.615
They are the documented output of a single institutional architecture that prioritises political control over military effectiveness.
